WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.717
A record labeled candidate clean has passed the technical checks selected for this exercise.

00:00:06.717 --> 00:00:13.347
That is useful, but it does not mean every value has been verified against the real world.

00:00:13.347 --> 00:00:21.727
A review status means the record contains missing, invalid, unsupported, or unresolved information.

00:00:21.727 --> 00:00:27.939
The duplicate rank helps us compare candidate records, but it does not prove identity.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:36.266
For example, an email can have a valid structure, a phone can have ten digits, and a date can parse correctly,

00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:40.031
yet the information can still belong to the wrong person.

00:00:40.031 --> 00:00:46.486
Technical validation improves consistency. It does not automatically establish truth.

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:54.431
That distinction is one of the most important professional habits in data work: describe exactly what your checks prove,

00:00:54.431 --> 00:00:57.308
and do not claim more than the evidence supports.
